{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>YHWH YHWH.</b> Rashi explains: one before he sins and one after he sins. That is, regarding the calf — i.e., idolatry — where the Holy One, blessed be He, joins thought to deed, it is written with ה' ה' — once before he sins, for he is liable for the thought as for the deed, as it is written regarding idolatry: 'למען תפוש את בני ישראל בלבם' (to catch the children of Israel in their hearts). But regarding the spies, who are not liable for thought before deed but only after the deed, as it is written: 'און אם ראית בלבי לא ישמע ה' (if you saw iniquity in my heart, may YHWH not hear it)' — there it is not written ה' but only once." "<b>El.</b> A judge and magistrate, as in 'עד האלהים יבא דבר שניהם' (the matter of both shall come before the Elohim)." "<b>Rachum.</b> Has compassion on the poor and the suffering — this is the attribute of mercy." "<b>Vechanun.</b> Applies even to the wealthy, as it is said: 'וצדיק חונן ונותן' (and a righteous man shows grace and gives), 'יחנך בני' (may He show you grace, my son), 'ויחנך' (and may He show you grace)." "<b>Erech apayim.</b> An expression of waiting, as in 'וארכא בחיין יהיבת להון' (and length of life was given to them), of Daniel, and in Old French, disbeitint; the vernacular lonkairish is mistaken. <b>Erech apayim:</b> I do not hasten to exact payment from the wicked — perhaps they will repent of themselves; and for the righteous, I lengthen My forbearance to exact payment from them, and I increase My anger upon them, in order to merit them for the life of the World to Come. Another interpretation: <b>Erech apayim</b> — for as long as I wish, I can take My vengeance; but a human being is not long of forbearance, rather he is quick to take his vengeance, for if he is here today, tomorrow he is in the grave." "<b>And abundant kindness.</b> Just as we find that the measure of goodness is greater than the measure of punishment." "<b>And truth.</b> That He fulfills what He promises."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:54.089096957Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}